      "message": "Unfortunately no. Imagine the cache holds a store at %50, containing the value associated with `myVec4`. Now there is a store into %60, which is a non-memory object, specifically an OpAccessChain to `myVec4.z`. Storing into %60 invalidates the cached store at %50. Unfortunately we don\u0027t track the relationship between %50 and %60.\n\nI do realize, though, that we could clear the cache first, and then emit the OpStore. We do know the value at %60 with confidence.",
